    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0315" n="239" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1937</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Clerk Brewer, in charge of the Legation
                        archives</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-28T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 28, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 24 and 26. Do you think American forces have situation sufficiently
                    under control to prevent future outbreaks without declaration martial law? Would
                    immediate declaration martial law in capital or throughout Republic have
                    satisfactory or unsatisfactory effect on present situation?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
